---------------- SSH client to the remote EC2 instance ----------------

1. sudo apt-get update

2. Then for running multiple services of docker and we want to run it through by a single file and run simultaneously so there we have docker-compose.yml
// sudo apt-get install docker.io docker-compose 

3. Now we need to give the permissions to the docker and append it into the docker group;  
// sudo usermod -aG docker $USER

4. Then just refersh the docker group
// newgrp docker

5. ubuntu@ip-172-31-3-251:~$ docker compose version
Docker Compose version 2.40.3+ds1-0ubuntu1
ubuntu@ip-172-31-3-251:~$ docker --version
Docker version 29.1.3, build 29.1.3-0ubuntu4.1

6. Before we run the ./start.sh shell file we need to set this as an ENV variable in our EC2 system :- 
// export PUBLIC_HOST=3.110.118.143 (EC2 Public IPv4 Address)
// And we can see all the variable there as well by below command
// printenv 
// Then run shell file
// ./start.sh

7. After spining up the containers on EC2 instance now we need to add inbound rules for EC2 instance in the security group
// 3000 port; for Elastiflix Frontend; Source type: Anywhere-IPv4
// 5601 port; for Kibana; Source type: My IP
// 9200 port; for ElasticSearch; Source type: My IP
// 17700 port; for Elastiflix Backend; Source type: Anywhere-IPv4

8. Then copy the IPv4 address of the EC2 instance and access via it for the frontend app running on port: 3000 and backend on port: 17700
// e.g. http://15.206.210.132:3000
// http://15.206.210.132:17700

----------------------------------------------------------------------